WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.525
Cross-tenant synchronization
pushes the partner's

2
00:00:03.525 --> 00:00:07.162
internal members into the
agency tenant as B2B users.

3
00:00:07.162 --> 00:00:11.985
Allow it only when every condition holds
and is written in the exception record:

4
00:00:11.985 --> 00:00:15.639
the partner's people are internal
members of an Entra tenant,

5
00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:19.951
the population is too large or changes
too fast for per-person requests,

6
00:00:19.951 --> 00:00:23.385
the agreement covers privacy,
consent and minimization,

7
00:00:23.385 --> 00:00:26.674
and the business owner decides,
with the sponsor named.

8
00:00:26.674 --> 00:00:29.061
The agency doesn't own the mappings,

9
00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:32.188
so it states them as terms
and tests the result.

10
00:00:32.188 --> 00:00:34.902
The user type mapping defaults to member;

11
00:00:34.902 --> 00:00:37.776
the profile requires
guest, applied always.

12
00:00:37.776 --> 00:00:42.238
Matching uses the alternative security
identifier and can't be changed.

13
00:00:42.238 --> 00:00:47.974
The deletion threshold defaults to 500,
so set it below the expected population.

14
00:00:47.974 --> 00:00:50.225
A failing job goes into quarantine.

15
00:00:50.225 --> 00:00:54.837
Scope only assigned users and
groups; nested groups don't cascade.

16
00:00:54.837 --> 00:01:00.350
And cycles run every 40 minutes, so
emergency suspension can't wait for one.

17
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:04.850
Sync creates the account; access
still comes from an access package.
